  "live_records": {
    "q-109861": {
      "dom_id": "step-q109861",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Let $A$ and $B$ be $m\\times p$ and $p\\times n$ matrices, respectively. What is the image of $\\text{Col}({B}^{T}\\,{A}^{T})$ under the action of $AB?$",
      "worked_solution": "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ by $AB$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $AB:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ (ab)_{1} & (ab)_{2} & ⋯ & (ab)_{n} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{AB}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (ab)_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (ab)_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{n}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (ab)_{n} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $AB$ must be $\\text{Col}(AB),$ the column space of $AB.$\n\nFurthermore, since $\\text{Null}(AB)$ is mapped to the zero vector $0$ by the definition of the null subspace, the image of its orthogonal complement $\\text{Col}((AB)^{T})=\\text{Col}({B}^{T}\\,{A}^{T})$ must be $\\text{Col}(AB).$\n\nThis can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14284843/assets/885bf8a3061f93ad400897a7273ffe4157d22dee20b8e4ee7ebb982b1c4319bb.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-109861-a",
